    "narrative": "For the July 21 slate, the focal point of the LawDog lineup is **Bryce Harper**, who leads our starters with a strong 68.07 rating. His matchup against Wrobleski is highly favorable, bolstered by a 0.386 xwOBA and a positive park/SP skill synergy that makes him our most reliable asset. **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.94) and **Gleyber Torres** (65.68) follow closely as elite plays; **Jung Hoo Lee** benefits significantly from a dynamic platoon advantage against Avila, while **Gleyber Torres** enjoys an offensive lift from his leadoff spot and a strong platoon edge against Peterson. While we are tracking a 42% rain risk for **Gleyber Torres**, his efficiency score remains high enough to warrant a start given his current form. Meanwhile, **Masyn Winn** (61.69) serves as a strategic play, specifically highlighted for his potential to swipe bags against a slower delivery, which aligns perfectly with our organizational priority on speed.\n\nThe decision to bench **JJ Bleday** was the closest call of the morning, with his 46.11 score narrowly falling behind our lower-tier starters. While **JJ Bleday** provides some utility, the optimizer favored the platoon advantages found in **Gavin Sheets** and **Jonathan Aranda**, the latter of whom posted a solid 60.01 score against Gausman despite the pitcher's talent level. We are monitoring **Cal Raleigh** and **Lawrence Butler** closely as their lineups remain pending; should **Lawrence Butler** be dropped in the order, his utility may diminish further, but for now, his raw base projection keeps him in the mix. We remain cautious regarding **Kyle Karros**, whose 49.92 rating is bolstered by a favorable wind-out environment and a high park factor, though he must contend with a tough SP skill matchup against Palmquist. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** still sidelined, our depth is being tested, but the current configuration maximizes our remaining daily caps against this afternoon\u2019s pitching slate.",
